Do not remove files from the interim jdk.javadoc module while JVMs may start

The rule that copies the generated element lists into the exploded interim
module jdk.javadoc.interim first deletes what is in the target directory and
then copies the lists (busybox cp also unlinks a destination that exists).
Every JVM that the build starts with INTERIM_LANGTOOLS_ARGS has that module
on its module path and walks the module's directory to list its packages.
When a file disappears during that walk, the module finder takes the
directory for something that is not a module, and the JVM stops during
startup because it cannot find the module jdk.javadoc.interim.

The error text is left out here on purpose: patch prints this header into
every build log.  It is in the message of the commit that added this file.

Nothing orders jdk.javadoc-gendata, which runs this rule, against
jdk.compiler-gendata (ct.sym) or the Java compilations, which start such
JVMs, so the build can fail by chance.

Only add the files that are not there yet; nothing is removed or replaced.
The interim module then keeps the four lists that the interim compilation
copied from the source tree, which the rule used to delete.  A list that is
already there is not copied again.  A package build starts with an empty
build directory, so it has no old list to keep; an incremental build in the
same directory would keep one.

Not upstream: openjdk/jdk master and jdk17u still have the rule as it was
(checked 2026-11-17).

--- a/make/modules/jdk.javadoc/Gendata.gmk
+++ b/make/modules/jdk.javadoc/Gendata.gmk
@@ -104,10 +104,15 @@
 INTERIM_JDK_JAVADOC_DIR := $(BUILDTOOLS_OUTPUTDIR)/interim_langtools_modules/jdk.javadoc.interim
 INTERIM_ELEMENT_LISTS_DIR := $(INTERIM_JDK_JAVADOC_DIR)/$(ELEMENT_LISTS_PKG)
 
+# Only add the files that are missing: nothing may disappear from this
+# exploded module, not even for a moment, while a JVM that has it on its
+# module path starts.
 $(INTERIM_JDK_JAVADOC_DIR)/_element_lists.marker: $(JDK_JAVADOC_DIR)/_element_lists.marker
 	$(call MakeDir, $(INTERIM_ELEMENT_LISTS_DIR))
-	$(RM) -r $(INTERIM_ELEMENT_LISTS_DIR)/*
-	$(CP) -R $(ELEMENT_LISTS_DIR)/* $(INTERIM_ELEMENT_LISTS_DIR)/
+	for f in $(ELEMENT_LISTS_DIR)/*; do \
+	  [ -e $(INTERIM_ELEMENT_LISTS_DIR)/$${f##*/} ] || \
+	      $(CP) $$f $(INTERIM_ELEMENT_LISTS_DIR)/ || exit 1; \
+	done
 	$(TOUCH) $@
 
 ################################################################################
